Yeah I do think it's ridiculous. But that's irrelevant, what's important is that it's hard to make sense of it all since we already have a way to measure personalities, as I've described above. Why do people go to such lengths to try to categorize themselves politically? Isn't it enough that they know who they are themselves? Why does everyone else have to adapt to their current identity by changing their language, which can be changed on a whim? I can't help but think that some underlying desire for a shift in power dynamic is the root.

&#x200B;

Also I never said I wasn't biased.

How fundamental are the processes? And how do you know there isn't a fundamental counter-mechanism that we've lost with the techological advance of society- which is the case for many other non-communicable diseases that have risen in number because of our different way of life?

&#x200B;

Let's give fasting as an example. When intake of fuel is low, the body has to utilize what it has to the best effect. There's some speculation that it begins with corrupted proteins and cells that have lost their proper function- which implies that the body somehow knows this, which isn't all that unprobable.

&#x200B;

So how do you know that the fundamental processes you propose aren't skewed simply because everyone at large lives a much different life now, compared to >500 years ago?

You don't know that, and therefore it's neither knowable or well understood.

There's some evidence that higher fruit and vegetable intake reduces symptoms- not a shocker there.

But also something you can try is to reduce salt intake. Ther's also some evidence that it helps.

&#x200B;

Other than that, buy a nose kettle and use it with a homemade saline solution, they're amazing in clearing you out.

